V4_8 RELEASE NOTES

* Added ehr5.dat and corresponding netCDF files.
  - At the same time, changed the naming convention for hionize, etc.

* Added adaswrite code and corresponding ADAS subroutine for reading adf11 files.

* Added efit2dg2d code and associated subroutines for setting up midplane tokamak geometries.
  - Included a Python script that plots the resulting "polygons".

* Established the concept of "external reactions" in problemsetup so that DEGAS 2 can be
  used to handle impurity ion ionization and recombination data, not just proceseses
  involving neutral species (for coupling to XGC0).

* Removed the "particle velocity vector" tally from source code and examples,
  - Originally introduced to compute an average velocity vector by dividing the flux vector by
    the density,
  - However, the "divide number" conversion used to carry out that task was found to be incompatible
    with having multiple source groups.
  - With the removal of "divide number", "particle velocity vector" tally was rendered
    equivalent to "neutral flux vector", allowing the former to be removed.

* Fixed a number of minor issues flagged by the Intel compiler.

* Completely removed the sector based sheath parameters,
  - This information is now contained in equivalent miscellaneous source parameters.
  - One consequence of this is that defineback (and boxgen, readbackground) will only update the
    geometry netCDF file in problems having BGK (neutral-neutral) reactions and vacuum zones.
    I.e., rarely.

* Updated problem input files in several of the examples to provide users a set of
  "best available" reaction lists for the most common situations,
  - Added a corresponding "best practices" sub-section to the User's Manual (in the
    "Atomic Physics" section).

* Updated the estimators used in the "REACTION" section of the example tally input files to
  reflect current usage,
  - Each now has the current list of reaction plus source types,
  - And post-processing estimators have been replaced with track length wherever they give
    equivalent results.

* As a result of this, the change in problem input files, and the removal of the "particle 
  velocity vector" tally, virtually all of the example output netCDF files have been updated.

* Added a macro option to postdetector to write out data as function of distance along a chord.

* Imported from SOLPS-ITER a few changes to DG to allow it to work with 64 bit systems,
  - Made corresponding changes to the Makefile.

* Remedied a couple of FWEB problems reported by users,
  - An updated distribution is now available on the FTP site; see the FWEB section of
    the User's Manual.

* Added to the Doc directory a detailed description of the UEDGE-DEGAS2 coupling procedure.

* Added to the Doc directory this RELEASE_NOTES file, including all Git log information.


